---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { colorionHref } from '../data/colorion';
import { effects } from '../data/buttons';
---
<Layout title="About the CSS button library and MIT license | Colorion" description="Learn about Colorion’s free CSS button library, its code exports, MIT license, and how to report an issue." breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Buttons', href: '/' }, { name: 'About & license', href: '/about/' }]}>
  <main class="page-width content-main" id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">About the library</span><h1>Small effects. Open code.</h1><p>A Colorion collection of {effects.length} button effects built with HTML and CSS. Try them, learn how they work, and adapt them to your interface.</p></div><article class="prose"><h2>What you can copy</h2><p>Every gallery example includes a complete CSS export and an agent prompt. Selected implementations also have dedicated pages with separate HTML, CSS, and React examples. The effects need no JavaScript animation library.</p><p>Focus styles and reduced-motion rules travel with the exported CSS. You still need to test your own colors, surrounding layout, browser targets, and interaction states.</p><h2>Who maintains it</h2><p>The library is part of <a href={colorionHref('https://colorion.co/')}>Colorion</a>. The source is available in <a href="https://github.com/ckissi/colorion-animated-buttons">the project’s GitHub repository</a>. Use the repository to report a broken example or suggest a correction.</p><h2>Use the code under MIT</h2><p>The <a href="/license.txt">MIT license</a> permits personal and commercial use, modification, and redistribution. Keep the copyright and license notice with copies or substantial portions of the code. The software comes without a warranty.</p><h2>Related tools</h2><p>Find color ideas in <a href={colorionHref('https://colorpalettes.colorion.co/')}>Colorion Palettes</a>, compare <a href={colorionHref('https://gradientbuttons.colorion.co/')}>gradient buttons</a>, or explore <a href={colorionHref('https://kinetics.colorion.co/')}>spring and pointer motion in Kinetics</a>.</p><h2>Make an example your own</h2><p>Start with a <a href="/collections/">button collection</a>, read the <a href="/guides/">implementation guides</a>, or use the <a href="/tools/button-generator/">button generator</a>.</p></article></main>
</Layout>
